# {{project_name}}

A MuduDB application written in C#, compiled to a WebAssembly component with
componentize-dotnet and packaged as `{{module_name}}.mpk`. Scaffolded with
`mpm-crate` — edit this project freely; it is a starting point, not a
generated artifact.

It defines three tables (`items`, `item_info`, `item_info_labels`, see
`sql/ddl.sql`) and two Mudu Procedures (see `src/Procedures.cs`):
`create_item` (scalar arguments) and `update_item_info`, which demonstrates
a **user-defined record type** — the `item-info` record declared in
`wit/types.wit` — as a procedure parameter and return type.

## Prerequisites

- .NET 10 SDK (10.0.400 or later) on PATH as `dotnet`; override with
  `DOTNET=/path/to/dotnet cargo make`.
- NuGet feeds (already in `nuget.config`): nuget.org plus
  `dotnet-experimental` (hosts
  `BytecodeAlliance.Componentize.DotNet.Wasm.SDK` and the pinned
  `runtime.linux-x64.Microsoft.DotNet.ILCompiler.LLVM` runtime pack).
- `cargo-make` (`cargo install cargo-make`) and `wasm-tools` (`cargo install
  wasm-tools`).
- `mgen`, `mtp`, `mpm-build` — the MuduDB toolchain; `mpm-install`, `mudud`,
  `mcli` to install and invoke the package.

## Layout

- `sql/ddl.sql` — database schema; `sql/init.sql` — seed data.
- `src/Procedures.cs` — hand-written procedures; SQL runs through
  `src/MuduSys.cs` (MSSP framing) over the `mududb:api/system` byte pipe.
  Each procedure is a `public static` method with a `// mudu-proc` comment
  immediately above it (only whitespace between the comment and the
  method); the first parameter is the `MuduOid` session. Parameter types:
  `long` (I64), `string` (String), `double` (F64), `bool` (I32), `byte[]`
  (Binary), and the user-defined record types of `wit/types.wit` (used as
  `ItemInfo`). Result types: `long`, `string`, `double`, `bool`, `byte[]`
  and the record types.
- `wit/types.wit` — the project's message types (the `item-info` record),
  consumed two ways: `mgen message` turns it into the C# structs/formatters
  under `src/types/`, and `mtp --type-wit` registers the names so procedure
  signatures may use them. The `package` clause is required: one WIT
  directory is one package.
- `src/types/Types.cs` — **generated by mgen** (`cargo make gentypes`): the
  `ItemInfo` struct plus its `ItemInfoFormatter` MessagePack codec, in the
  `{{pascal_name}}Types` namespace (mgen sanitizes dots in `--namespace`,
  so the template passes the dot-free form). Never edit by hand.
- `src/WorldExportsImpl.cs` — **generated by mtp** (`cargo make transpile`):
  the `{{pascal_name}}World.{{pascal_name}}WorldExportsImpl` exports class
  implementing the `mp2-*` world exports: decodes `UniProcedureParam`,
  dispatches to `Procedures`, encodes the result. One `Mp2<PascalProc>`
  method per procedure; record parameters decode through the per-type
  `As<Name>` helper (`MuduSys.RecordFieldValues` composed with the
  generated formatter), record results through
  `MuduSys.EncodeProcedureOkRecord`. Never edit by hand.
- `src/MiniMsgPack.cs` — the minimal MessagePack codec the wire format needs.
- `src/MuduSys.cs` — the syscall layer plus the record bridge
  (`RecordFieldValues` / `EncodeProcedureOkRecord`) transcoding between the
  positional record-case envelope and the generated formatters' field maps.
- `src/items.cs` — the `items` entity record, its SQL statements and the
  `MuduSys` row codecs (`InsertParams`/`FromRow`), **generated by
  `mgen entity`** from `sql/ddl.sql` on every build (one `<table>.cs` per
  table, in the global namespace; do not edit by hand).
- `wit/world.wit` — **generated by mtp**: the component world, `import
  mududb:api/system` plus one `mp2-<kebab-proc>` export per procedure.
  `wit/deps/mududb-api/api.wit` is a copy of the host syscall interface.
- `package/package.cfg.json` — package metadata.
- `package/package.desc.json` — **generated by mtp**: the procedure
  signatures. PascalCase method names and camelCase parameter names
  normalize to the snake_case wire form (`CreateItem` → `create_item`,
  `itemId` → `item_id`); a record parameter is described with the host's
  `Record` type family, the WIT field names verbatim as the JSON keys.

Adding a procedure means writing the method plus its `// mudu-proc` marker
and rebuilding — the exports class, the world WIT and the descriptor stay in
sync because all three come from the same source.

## Build

```bash
cargo make package
```

This runs `mgen entity` → `mgen message` (gentypes) → `mtp csharp`
(transpile) → `mgen check-sql` → `dotnet build -c
Release` (restore → compile → componentize) → `wasm-tools validate` →
`mpm-build create`, producing
`target/wasm32-wasip2/release/{{module_name}}.mpk`. The component file is
named `{{module_name}}.wasm` so its stem matches the `{{module_name}}`
module in `package/package.desc.json` (an `mpm-build` requirement).

The generated record codecs and the mtp adapter use only the raw
`MessagePackReader`/`MessagePackWriter` paths of the `MessagePack` package —
WASI-safe. The static `MessagePackSerializer` paths are NOT (their
`MessagePackSecurity` static initializer needs a random-number generator
WASI does not provide); do not call them in guest code.

## Install and invoke

Start `mudud`, then:

```bash
mpm-install target/wasm32-wasip2/release/{{module_name}}.mpk

mcli --addr 127.0.0.1:9527 --http-addr 127.0.0.1:8300 app-invoke \
  --app {{module_name}} --module {{module_name}} --proc create_item \
  --json '{"item_id": 2, "name": "pear"}'
```

## Records on the wire

A record argument travels as the positional `uni-data-value` record case
(field order = WIT declaration order, names dropped by the host); the guest
side never touches that envelope by hand — the mtp-generated adapter decodes
it through the record bridge (`MuduSys.RecordFieldValues`) composed with the
mgen-generated `ItemInfoFormatter`, and encodes a record result
symmetrically (`MuduSys.EncodeProcedureOkRecord`). Rules of the JSON/desc
surface:

- **JSON keys = WIT field names, verbatim** (`in-stock`, not `inStock`).
- **Booleans cross as 0/1** — the host has no boolean data-type family, so
  a WIT `bool` field is described as `I32` and takes JSON `0`/`1`.
- **u32/u16/u8 fields cross as i32**; missing JSON fields are an error,
  unknown keys are tolerated.

Invoke the record procedure with nested JSON:

```bash
mcli --addr 127.0.0.1:9527 --http-addr 127.0.0.1:8300 app-invoke \
  --app {{module_name}} --module {{module_name}} --proc update_item_info \
  --json '{"item_id": 2, "info": {"name": "pear", "price": 250, "in-stock": 1, "labels": ["fruit", "fresh"]}}'
```

`update_item_info` stores the record flattened into the `item_info` table
(the label list as `item_info_labels` side rows keyed by `(item_id, idx)`)
and returns the rebuilt record, updating the row by key and inserting it
on first write.

C# v1 limits for user-defined types: no `option<T>` procedure types yet;
`binary`/`list<u8>` record fields are rejected (declare them as `blob`
instead).

## Extending

- Add a procedure: write another `public static` method with its
  `// mudu-proc` marker in `src/Procedures.cs` and rebuild.
- Add a record type: declare it in `wit/types.wit`, rebuild — `src/types/`
  regenerates and the type becomes usable in procedure signatures.
- Add a table: extend `sql/ddl.sql`, rebuild, and use the regenerated
  entity (`src/<table>.cs`); `mgen check-sql` validates every SQL string
  literal against the schema on every build.
